# SQL migrations are checksummed byte-for-byte by `sqlx::migrate!` at compile
# time. CRLF changes that checksum and makes the daemon panic with
# Migrate(VersionMismatch) against a DB that recorded the LF checksum. Force LF
# regardless of the machine's core.autocrlf.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Shell scripts run under Git Bash; a CR in the shebang/commands breaks them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# `gofmt -l` reports every CRLF file as unformatted, so with core.autocrlf=true —
# the Windows default, and set globally on this machine — a plain checkout fails
# the fmt gate on files nobody touched. The blobs are already LF; this stops the
# checkout from undoing that, and is why CI does not need to normalise them first.
*.go text eol=lf

# A workflow bundle's IDENTITY is the hash of its bytes — that is what makes
# `autopilot/1.0.0` mean one thing and what `workflows.rs` answers `drifted` with.
# These files are embedded with `include_str!`, so a CRLF checkout would give the
# same NucleOS version a different hash on two machines, and every start on one of
# them would report the built-in workflow as changed and restore it. Same failure
# the `*.sql` rule at the top prevents, one directory over.
core/assets/** text eol=lf
